module test.claim.live_deploy.observed_unhealthy_deploy_witness

// CLAIMS FOR DEPLOY-UNHEALTHY-1 -- the third occurrence of
// gunbc.recurring_failure_mode a_deploy_that_observes_its_own_service_cannot_repair_it. On
// 2026-10-15 22:4xZ the operator-approved main-tip prod apply at 87cf694fb90 refused at PLAN, with
// no mutation: "live_deploy: the deployment plan could not be derived from the host:
// service-process: refused -- could not observe the host: the process is active but /healthz
// refused: http client GET failed within the 240 s probe deadline derived from the serve wall
// limit; tailnet door cutover refused with no route effect: the cutover journal could not be read,
// so an interrupted cutover cannot be ruled out: read refused: reply undecodable: HTTP 502".
// Prod had been crash-looping since 2026-10-14 21:00Z -- a half-applied deploy, new binary over the
// OLD tree -- so systemd called the unit Active (a service in a restart flurry is Active) while
// /healthz refused, and the observation folded that pair into 'could not observe the host', the
// same arm as an unreachable host. The only modeled route to repair prod therefore required prod to
// be healthy. Recovery left the model again: the operator ran tree-sync's own ExecStart by hand.
//
// VALUES ARE SUPPLIED AT THE INTERFACE, which is what makes the decision testable without a host:
// the probe reply (curl's success bit and the stdout it wrote, with the status line curl appended),
// the member observations, the cutover journal read. The wet inhabitance claim
// (test.claim.live_deploy.observed_unhealthy_probe_wet_witness) puts a REAL listener answering 503
// behind the same fold and shows the shape supplied here is the shape the real probe yields.
//
// RED/GREEN, stated per claim (DESIGN 5: a discriminating red fails on main for its stated reason):
//   CLAIM 1  plans_a_replacement_over_an_answered_503_at_a_different_revision   RED ON MAIN: main
//            has no ProcessObservedUnhealthy constructor at all, so the observation these claims
//            supply does not exist there and this file does not evaluate. The same probe reply on
//            main arrived as MemberUnobservable and the WHOLE plan refused -- the ledger's third
//            occurrence, quoted above -- which is what the paired refusal-naming claims pin.
//   CLAIM 2  a transport failure still refuses                                  CONTROL: green on
//            main and green here (the row's guard that silence keeps refusing).
//   CLAIM 3  a body naming a release is that release even at 503                CONTROL for the
//            body reading (main read bodies the same way); the 503 CARRYING it is new here.
//   CLAIM 4  a 502 journal read still refuses with no route effect              CONTROL: green on
//            both -- facet (b) weakened nothing; the interrupted-cutover refusal stands verbatim.
//            Its companions witness the ordering that removes the cyclic precondition.

